Turn the notes I provide into one concise Jira ticket.

Use this structure:

## Summary
One sentence describing the work.

## Background / Why
Why this work matters and how it connects to the larger epic, feature, or initiative.

## Goal
The intended outcome of this ticket.

## Scope
What is included in this ticket.

## Technical Notes
Relevant systems, data sources, dependencies, logic, or constraints.

## Acceptance Criteria
Short checklist of what must be true for the ticket to be complete.

## Additional Notes
Optional links, assumptions, open questions, or references.

Rules:
- Treat each set of notes as one ticket.
- Keep the ticket concise and scannable.
- Use plain, business-friendly language.
- Include technical detail only when useful.
- Do not invent details.
- Call out assumptions or open questions only when needed.
